<p>For Vanta alternatives, compare Drata for a broad trust-management programme, Secureframe for clearly described compliance packages, and Sprinto for ongoing evidence and control workflows. Scrut suits a risk-and-compliance evaluation across entities; Thoropass is relevant when you want software and an auditor-led service together. Hyperproof deserves a look for shared controls and risk programmes managed across teams. There is no universal cheapest choice: most equivalent scopes require quotes, and audit fees can be separate. Keep Vanta if its existing integrations and evidence history work well. Validate the required framework, entities, controls and services before switching.</p>
<h2>Compare the whole programme, not just a dashboard</h2>
<p>Vanta alternatives are usually bought to collect evidence, coordinate controls, support audits or answer customer security reviews. Those are connected jobs, but the contracts do not always bundle them in the same way. One proposal might include a single framework and a trust centre; another might add auditor services, questionnaire allowances or multiple entities.</p>
